  "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $4$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+1}-4.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/7ef3c8f48902dda0c80fb5fbd3db74dee4cd3ea71c2711878911f6bb0090d730.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\sqrt{x+1}-4.$",
